  <items>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117240648">puban</headword>
      <description>[pu̟bɑṉ] Notes: a lady’s “bun” [?]. [NOTES: unclear, could be ‘bum’!]</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117242520">sgiubach</headword>
      <description>[sɡʹu̟bɑx] Quotation: currachd sgiubach. Notes: cheese-cutter (cap).</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117244392">spriodag</headword>
      <description>[spɾid̪ɑɡ] Notes: spark.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117246120">triodh</headword>
      <description>[t̪ɾwɣ] Notes: whooping cough. [NOTES: slipped under ‘triogh’.]</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117247992">brochan</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Tha brochan as an uchd aige. Notes: rough wheezing in the chest – like “cròchan” in Lewis.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117249648">currachd</headword>
      <description>Quotation: currachd-sgiubach [sɡʹu̟bɔx]. Notes: peaked cap, cheese-cutter. [NOTES: slipped under ‘currac’.]</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp117251664">griuthach</headword>
      <description>[ɡɾiu̟hɔx] Notes: measles.</description>
    </item>
  </items>
